    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d228">

                <pb facs="0413" n="343" sameAs="frus:frus1867p2/pg343"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>Mr. Campbell to Mr.
                        Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 9.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">New Orleans</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1867-01-02"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 2, 1867</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> * * * * * * *</p>
                <p>As it is by no means my desire to remain in this city, and may be neither
                    pleasant to me personally, nor profitable to the government, that I should again
                    wander by sea and by land on the inhospitable border of Mexico just now, permit
                    me to express my regret that I have not been authorized by the department to
                    return, at least temporarily, to my home.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to remain, sir, respectfully, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>LEWIS D. CAMPBELL.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
